# Copy to .env.local for local development. .env.local is gitignored and must
# never be committed; the real values live in the Vercel project settings.

# Supabase Postgres, via the shared *transaction* pooler on :6543.
#
# The role is `website`, not `postgres`: it holds SELECT on the two hiscores
# views and EXECUTE on the accounts functions, and nothing else. The port is
# :6543 (transaction mode) because serverless scales to many concurrent
# instances and session mode (:5432) would exhaust the free pooler budget.
# Transaction mode forbids named prepared statements — see lib/db.ts.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://website.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# OPTIONAL override. TLS is always verified: the pooler's certificate chains to
# a self-signed "Supabase Root 2021 CA" that no public trust store carries, so
# that root ships with the app in lib/supabase-ca.ts and is used by default.
# Set this only to override it -- a CA rotation that has to land before a
# deploy can. Paste the PEM, newlines and all.
# DATABASE_SSL_CA="-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\n...\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----"

# Cloudflare Turnstile. Registration FAILS CLOSED: with TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY
# unset, every registration is rejected with 400 { "error": "turnstile" }.
# Blank here on purpose - a file that can be pasted straight into a production
# environment must not be able to open the gate by accident. The secret is the
# half that matters and nothing in this repo holds a copy of it.
#
# The SITE key is public - it is rendered into the HTML of /register - so it
# has a shipped default (lib/account/site-key.ts) and this variable only needs
# setting to point the form at a different widget.
#
# Cloudflare's official test keys, which always pass and are **local dev only;
# never in production**, are:
#   TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/troubleshooting/testing/
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAAEoMC04y54IPJd-n

# OPTIONAL. A solved Turnstile token names the hostname it was solved on, and
# the token is refused unless that hostname is listed here. Unset means the
# built-in list -- zanaris.rs, www.zanaris.rs, zanaris.vercel.app, localhost,
# 127.0.0.1 -- and setting this REPLACES that list rather than adding to it, so
# spell out everything the environment needs. An entry may start `*.` to match
# subdomains (`*.vercel.app` matches a preview host, not `vercel.app` itself).
#
# When it is needed: a Vercel PREVIEW deployment serves /register and
# /account/login from `<branch>-<project>.vercel.app`, which is not on the
# built-in list, so registering or logging in on a preview fails the Turnstile
# check until this is set on the Preview environment.
# ALLOWED_TURNSTILE_HOSTNAMES=zanaris.rs,*.vercel.app,localhost

# Public origin of the site. Used as `metadataBase` in app/layout.tsx, so
# every relative URL in the page metadata resolves against the real host
# rather than the localhost Next guesses. Unset or malformed falls back to
# https://zanaris.rs.
SITE_URL=https://zanaris.rs

# The key the website session cookie is signed with (HMAC-SHA256). Generate one
# with:
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Blank here on purpose, and the consequences of leaving it blank are the whole
# design: with SESSION_SECRET unset (or shorter than 32 characters) nothing can
# be signed or verified, so /api/account/login answers 503 and every account
# page redirects to the login form. Nobody can log in. Fail closed.
#
# It also seeds the fake salt an unknown username gets, which is what stops the
# login endpoint being a username oracle.
#
# Rotating it logs everybody out at once — every existing cookie stops
# verifying — which is the emergency stop if one is ever leaked. Use a
# different value on Production and Preview: a preview deployment is not a
# place to mint production sessions.
SESSION_SECRET=
